course: dictionary
lesson: 4381
title: Habsburg: a name with a big story
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Habsburg is a name, so it starts with a capital letter. Names of people, families, places and countries all work this way. When you see a capital letter in the middle of a sentence, ask yourself: is this a name?
explain: «The Habsburgs were a royal family of Europe.» The word royal is your clue: the Habsburgs were a family of kings and rulers. The dictionary says they ruled Austria, the Holy Roman Empire, Spain and other lands for hundreds of years.
explain: Look at «the Habsburg Empire». Here Habsburg works like a describing word: it tells you which empire you mean, just as Roman tells you which empire in Roman Empire. The word after it, Empire, is the thing being described.
explain: The clue to the time is in the sentence too. The Habsburgs ruled from the Middle Ages until 1918. If a text mentions a year or a time, use it to check when a name belongs to the story.
fact: Habsburg is a name for a royal family of Europe.
fact: «Habsburg» is written with a capital letter because it is a name.
fact: The Habsburgs ruled Austria, the Holy Roman Empire, Spain and other lands for hundreds of years.
fact: The Habsburgs ruled from the Middle Ages until 1918.
fact: «Habsburg» can also describe something, as in «the Habsburg Empire».
exercise: What kind of word is Habsburg? | A kind of food | A colour | *A name | A sport
exercise: «The Habsburg Empire was very large.» In this sentence, what does Habsburg describe? | The king's horse | The river | The sea | *The empire
exercise: The Habsburgs ruled for hundreds of years, from the Middle Ages until which year? | 2018 | *1918 | 1066 | 1500
test: «The Habsburg family ruled for hundreds of years.» Why does Habsburg start with a capital letter? | Because it is a long word | Because it is an action word | *Because it is a name | Because it is a number
test: Which country did the Habsburgs rule, according to the dictionary? | *Austria | Egypt | Japan | China
exam: Jayden says Habsburg is just a word for a big castle. What is the right answer? | No, it is a sea near Europe | Yes, it is a castle on a hill | *No, Habsburg is a name for a royal family who ruled Austria and other lands | Yes, it is a river that flows through Spain
